From f41d5d6c7f5f7b5c17ae15da61f8abe276f7b876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oddlyspaced <oddlyspaced1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:22:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gralloc: silence -Wformat on the 32-bit variants

This tree logs uint64_t/int64_t with %lu/%ld throughout. That is correct on arm64,
where uint64_t is unsigned long, but wrong on arm32, where it is unsigned long long,
so -Werror,-Wformat fails only the 32-bit variants. libgrallocutils had 25 such sites
across gr_utils.cpp and gr_snap_helper.cpp; libgralloccore then failed the same way in
gr_dma_mgr.cpp, and there is no reason to think it stops there.

metroid is core_64_bit_only and never loads 32-bit native code, so the failing variants
cannot ship. Suppress once in qtidisplay_common_defaults, scoped to arch arm, instead of
patching module after module as each is discovered. The 64-bit build, which is the one
that actually runs, keeps -Wformat.

Every compiled module in the tree that sets -Werror inherits this defaults, directly or
via qtidisplay_defaults, except libhistogram and its two tools -- and those carry no
%lu/%ld at all, so they need nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RTyThMzCkh5fd3Ct1JP62p
Change-Id: Ic1e2ce7e69ddde5cd361bf9d016176eb484b626e
---
 Android.bp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 8ba1c9a..a6fb2d8 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -105,6 +105,17 @@ qtidisplay_cc_defaults {
         "-Wall",
         "-Werror",
     ],
+    // This tree logs uint64_t/int64_t with %lu/%ld throughout. Correct on arm64, where
+    // uint64_t is unsigned long; wrong on arm32, where it is unsigned long long. So
+    // -Werror,-Wformat fails only the 32-bit variants, in module after module.
+    // metroid is core_64_bit_only and never loads 32-bit native code, so those variants
+    // cannot ship. Suppress once here, for the arch that cannot ship, rather than
+    // per-module as each one is discovered. The 64-bit build keeps -Wformat.
+    arch: {
+        arm: {
+            cflags: ["-Wno-format"],
+        },
+    },
     shared_libs: [
         "liblog",
         "libcutils",
-- 
